turn _bundles(views_db, items_db, view_ids, as_of, coverage='library')\nrg: src/hivemind/store.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: src/hivemind/judge.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: src/hivemind/judging.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: src/hivemind/matching.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:19:def open_ledger(path):\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:178:def dependencies(conn, view_id, as_of):\nsrc/hivemind/service.py:193:def dependants(conn, view_id, as_of):\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '40,75p' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/RESULT.md; rg -n 'D51[\"'^0-9]|D368[''^0-9]'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | cut -c1-330 | head -22; rg -n 'newest|sort\\\\(' poc/ui/src -g '*.js' | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"## Missing for a daily production test\n1. A daily feed and start (the harvest tools exist; no schedule; the gap after 10-27 needs a plan).\n2. Publishing each finished day to the page, API and MCP together, keeping the last good copy on a failed day.\n3. Spend, stale-data and failed-day alerts; the replay's `--cap` can overshoot.\n\nAlex's to decide: where it runs (Docker has no outbound model calls under the VPN on this Mac), who tests, and the spend ceiling.\n\n## Recommendation and one test (consensus)\n1. **$0 first:** serve a copy of old-2's finished 09-20 store (43 questions, 42 open) with its articles locally on the page, API and\n   MCP, confirm all three show the same day and source links (the page silently keeps its embedded v34 copy if its fetch fails), and\n   Alex reads it for half an hour: would an analyst use this? Codex read the store through the shared reader (`bundle.py:225`): it\n   returns 09-20 and all 43 questions.\n2. **Only if he says yes:** build the daily wrapper (harvest → clean → append → replay one day → snapshot → publish) with its alerts,\n   rehearse it one day at a time over the harvested 09-21..09-27 with one deliberately failed day (about $0.60 at the measured rate),\n   then plan the gap after 10-27 and switch to real days.\n\n## Step 1 done (2026-11-20)\nAlex: \"做\". A copy of old-2's 09-20 store is served on the host: the page at http://127.0.0.1:8792/index.html, the API on 8790 and MCP\non 8791 (`poc/data/review-v118-old2-0920-2026-11-20/README.md`). Checked: the page fetched `/library` from 8790 (HTTP 200); the API's\n`/library` and MCP's `thesis_library` are byte-identical (09-20, 43 questions, 42 open); a question's detail shows its answer,\nreasoning, quotes and source links. $0. Waiting on Alex's read.\n615:- Changed by D51: consensus is not part of the design at all; third-party views stay evidence of their tier.\n821:- Changed by D51: B is re-judged when what it reads changed (its evidence, or a dependency's conclusion marked\n935:- Changed by D51: the views database has two model settings in Config (matching, re-judging); dependencies are\n1143:- Changed by D51: item 9's re-judging on succession comes back as a case of the one re-judging rule; Config's\n1214:- Changed by D51: Alex settled Claude's open items of the frozen views database (2026-10-21).\n1239:- Changed by D51: the two open items it added are settled (dependencies chosen from the views shown; the double\n1256:## D51 · 2026-10-21 · Claude's open items settled: one re-judging rule, dependencies chosen in the matching call, no consensus\n1435:- Changes: D14, D29, D46, D51 item 4 (who sets an answer at the due date is settled); the frozen views database (D48)\n1464:- Checked: Claude read the final verdict, pull mode, views database, system overview and Config against D51 and D54.\n1466:  (D54). Each trigger of the old draft has a place in the rebuilt design (re-judging, D51; freezing, D54; the rule for\n1589:- Changes: D42, D44, D46, D51, D57 (notes under each); the frozen universe, extraction and views database through this\n1687:- Alex, shown that re-judging was half the cost (a hot view re-judged after every item, each call carrying all its evidence): \"是的应该要一天一次\". Re-judging moves from each item's round to one round per day: the day's items are extracted, matched and written in sequence as before; after the last item, and before pull mode freezes \n3957:  Alex. Found on the way: the default Jev path chooses no dependencies although D51 has matching choose them.\n3960:## D368 · 2026-11-05 · Alex's answers to the seven items left open by the consolidation\n3970:     (D191 point 2); the matching step chooses a new thesis's dependencies (D51), which the default Jev path does not ask today.\n4363:- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step. D368 item 1 still holds for the next production extraction version.\n5428:## D480 · 2026-11-13 · Under choice 3, production's opening rule is probed with a price (D191 point 4, D368 item 1) on its stored requests (council consensus under D439)\n5432:  D191 point 4 include (\"好\"); D368 item 1 (\"这个你记住，我们要做\") ordered it built in the next extraction version, measured against v74i.\n6353:## D532 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the two filing decisions stand as traced, a common mechanism is not established; next a bounded $0 trace of the dependency lead under D368's direction (council consensus, reflection round 23)\n6365:- **A decision Claude had missed: D368 (Alex, 2026-11-05)** already directs that the matching step's choice of a new thesis's\n6369:  system against the stored relationships between the questions concerned, the direction D368 gives, the dependency's\n6371:  reported as valid under D368, figure present in that conclusion, or unavailable or ambiguous. **Stop** if no directionally\npoc/ui/src/model/trigger.js:16:    Object.keys(condition).sort().join(',') !== 'operator,threshold' ||\npoc/ui/src/model/market.js:10:    Object.keys(value).sort().join(',') !== 'allocation,range' ||\npoc/ui/src/model/market.js:25:    Object.keys(value).sort().join(',') !==\npoc/ui/src/model/market.js:63:/** Anchor ranges to the newest observation, independently of the thesis replay date. */\npoc/ui/src/model/market.js:66:  const latest = [snapshot.hourly.at(-1), snapshot.daily.at(-1)].sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]).at(-1);\npoc/ui/src/model/library.js:32:    .sort((a, b) => {\npoc/ui/src/model/graph.js:42:    if (!edge || Object.keys(edge).sort().join(',') !== 'sourceId,targetId')\npoc/ui/src/components/canvas.js:49:      : [data.days[0] || data.as_of, addDays(data.as_of, -30)].sort().at(-1);\npoc/ui/src/components/thes