19; push toward_last] AMD reported 37% higher overall SPEC 2026 performance for 192-core 5th Gen EPYC CPUs and 2.37x performance for 256-core 6th Gen EPYC Venice versus NVIDIA Vera. | source: AMD Targets NVIDIA Vera In Latest EPYC Venice “Agentic AI” Benchmarks, Zen 6 Leads With 20% Higher Per-Core & Over 2x Gains In Platform-Level Performance (wccftech.com) input gnews:83ffa482f76b03da59ac2674\n  - e5051 [party_statement; 2026-09-19; push toward_last] AMD reported EPYC 9006 CPUs achieved a 12% per-core performance gain in Agentic AI benchmarks, averaging 20% in the a4 subtests. | source: AMD Targets NVIDIA Vera In Latest EPYC Venice “Agentic AI” Benchmarks, Zen 6 Leads With 20% Higher Per-Core & Over 2x Gains In Platform-Level Performance (wccftech.com) input gnews:83ffa482f76b03da59ac2674\n  - e5052 [party_statement; 2026-09-19; push toward_last] AMD’s Agentic AI benchmark results showed EPYC Venice up to 2.01x faster per core in stockfish_r, with a lead above 30% in many tests against NVIDIA Vera. | source: AMD Targets NVIDIA Vera In Latest EPYC Venice “Agentic AI” Benchmarks, Zen 6 Leads With 20% Higher Per-Core & Over 2x Gains In Platform-Level Performance (wccftech.com) input gnews:83ffa482f76b03da59ac2674\n  - e5053 [party_statement; 2026-09-19; push toward_last] AMD reported EPYC Venice had 18% faster memory bandwidth than NVIDIA Vera, with 1.6 TB/s versus 1.2 TB/s of platform bandwidth. | source: AMD Targets NVIDIA Vera In Latest EPYC Venice “Agentic AI” Benchmarks, Zen 6 Leads With 20% Higher Per-Core & Over 2x Gains In Platform-Level Performance (wccftech.com) input gnews:83ffa482f76b03da59ac2674\n  - e5054 [party_statement; 2026-09-19; push toward_last] AMD reported that EPYC Venice’s 96 cores had access to 8% more memory bandwidth per core than NVIDIA Vera’s 88 cores. | source: AMD Targets NVIDIA Vera In Latest EPYC Venice “Agentic AI” Benchmarks, Zen 6 Leads With 20% Higher Per-Core & Over 2x Gains In Platform-Level Performance (wccftech.com) input gnews:83ffa482f76b03da59ac2674\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n  - e795 [third_party_view; 2026-07-22] BofA expects AMD's AI 2026 Day on Thursday to focus less on benchmark comparisons and more on establishing the industry's preferred metric for AI infrastructure performance. | source: BofA sees server CPU TAM hitting $170bn by 2030 as NVIDIA takes on AMD (au.finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:55b3b854d30ecb73679c2088\n  - e2715 [party_statement; 2026-08-26] NVIDIA had said it expected CPU sales to reach $20 billion in the current fiscal year, FY2027. | source: Jensen Huang Just Delivered Great News to Nvidia Shareholders (fool.com) input gnews:58da18a5e0a271a50e9bbdaf\n  - e4796 [fact; 2026-09-16] NVIDIA Grace CPU revenue exceeded $5 billion over the trailing twelve months. | source: Why It’s Time to Load Up on Nvidia Stock (barchart.com) input gnews:5c5a96c670714dee86769d87\n  - e597 [party_statement; 2026-07-18] NVIDIA projected that the data-center CPU market could reach $200 billion in the next few years. | source: Nvidia: Jensen Huang's Company Is Still the King of AI, and the Stock Is a Buy (fool.com) input gnews:24a3f9f56a73a4f25edfd458\n  - e681 [party_statement; 2026-07-21] NVIDIA management said the Vera CPU opens a $200 billion total addressable market for NVIDIA; no period was specified. | source: The Two Radically Different Futures Priced Into NVIDIA Stock (trefis.com) input gnews:53839087525ebaad78aef90b\n\n## v21: How much will NVIDIA's total revenue grow in FY2027?\n\n- Looks at: NVIDIA total revenue growth in FY2027\n- Opened 2026-07-26 from: Is Micron a Better Artificial Intelligence (AI) Stock Than Nvidia? (fool.com); due 2027-02-28; open\n- Research groups: none\n- Answer ladder:\n  1. Strongly bullish: FY2027 total revenue growth is at least 60%.  <== current\n  2. Bullish: FY2027 total revenue growth is at least 50% and below 60%.\n  3. Neutral: FY2027 total revenue growth is at least 35% and below 50%, bracketing Wall Street's 42% estimate cited in the item.\n  4. Bearish: FY2027 total revenue growth is at least 20% and below 35%.\n  5. Strongly bearish: FY2027 total revenue growth is below 20%.\n- History: 50 judgements; first judged 2026-07-26 at rung 3; rung moves: 2026-07-29 3->2, 2026-07-31 2->1\n- Latest judgement 2026-09-20, why changed: The newer consensus figures remain near the previous 87–90% reference, and the implied run-rate remains about $407 billion, or roughly 88% growth. The quantified estimate of more than $100 billion in unmet AI-infrastructure demand is broader than NVIDIA revenue and does not change the implied figure; the CFO's approximately 70% outlook is consistent with the prior lower-growth check.\n- Latest reasoning: The market reference is roughly 87–90% FY2027 growth (Zacks estimates 87.4–88%, while the $411 billion estimate implies about 90% against FY2026 revenue), which is rung 1; the ladder's cited 42% estimate is not the current reference. Q1 and Q2 revenue plus Q3 guidance total $285.8 billion. Carrying forward the approximately 12% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance gives Q4 revenue of about $121 billion, FY2027 revenue near $407 billion, and growth of about 88% from FY2026's $215.94 billion. The CFO's approximately 70% growth outlook implies about $367 billion, also rung 1. Supplier constraints temper the faster run-rate case, but the reported results and Q3 guide still imply growth well above the 60% boundary.\n- Evidence in force: 124 (third_party_view 54, fact 39, party_statement 31)\n- Evidence cited by the latest judgement:\n  - e1883 [fact; 2026-08-15; push none] NVIDIA reported FY2026 total revenue of $215.94 billion, up 65.47% year over year. | source: The 4 Words From Jensen Huang That Could Redefine NVIDIA’s Total Addressable Market (247wallst.com) input gnews:3ef8c07472c4da3ddb8d4350\n  - e2146 [fact; 2026-08-19; push toward_first] NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 first-quarter revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, about $2 billion above the top of its earlier $78.0 billion-plus-or-minus-2% guidance range; Data Center revenue was $75.2 billion, up 92%. | source: Nvidia Guided to $91 Billion. Wall Street Penciled In $92 Billion. (fool.com) input gnews:712a161a59386d843542f6ac\n  - e2497 [fact; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 18% quarter over quarter and 106% year over year. | source: NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027 | NVIDIA Newsroom (NVIDIA Corporation) input nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027\n  - e2499 [party_statement; 2026-08-26; push toward_first] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, assuming no Data Center compute revenue from China. | source: NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027 | NVIDIA Newsroom (NVIDIA Corporation) input nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027\n  - e3943 [party_statement; 2026-09-04; push toward_first] NVIDIA's FY2027 Q3 guidance implied total revenue growth of 12% sequentially at the midpoint. | source: Jensen Huang's Nvidia Guided for 70% Revenue Growth in Fiscal 2028, Far Above the 44% Wall Street Expected, as Amazon Agreed to Buy 2 Million Nvidia GPUs. Is the Growth Forecast Believable? (fool.com) input gnews:89698c9955cf8aa35b642970\n  - e3108 [party_statement; 2026-08-28; push toward_last] CFO Colette Kress guided to 70% growth for NVIDIA revenue for the full fiscal year; the article says this was ahead of analyst estimates. | source: Jim Cramer Explained What Turned The Tide For NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA)’s Stock (finance.yahoo.com) input gnews:b39d8c4b1f73b622347a66e4\n  - e4702 [third_party_view; 2026-09-14; push toward_first] Zacks consensus estimates NVIDIA FY2027 total revenue growth of 87.4% year over year and EPS growth of 93.5%. | source: NVIDIA vs. Marvell: Which AI Infrastructure Stock Is the Better Buy? (zacks.com) input gnews:1d3bc1ba4c2df5e998884bdb\n  - e4822 [third_party_view; 2026-09-16; push toward_first] Analysts forecast NVIDIA revenue growth of 88% in FY2027 and 65.5% in FY2028; they forecast earnings growth of 93.5% and 66%, respectively. | source: Zacks Industry Outlook NVIDIA, Texas, STMicroelectronics and Intel (zacks.com) input gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182\n  - e4348 [third_party_view; 2026-09-10; push toward_first] Analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $411 billion in FY2027 and $678 billion in FY2028, implying 65% FY2028 growth. | source: Nvidia Has $96 Billion in Quarterly Revenue. Here's Why the Stock Is Still a Buy. (fool.com) input gnews:90f3858225bf7e19b8f38f21\n  - e4900 [party_statement; 2026-09-18; push toward_last] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA expected revenue to grow approximately 70% next year because of supply constraints. | source: Analysis: What Nvidia’s Massive Supply-Demand Gap Says About AI Mania (crn.com) input gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33\n  - e4901 [third_party_view; 2026-09-18; push toward_last] CRN estimated that NVIDIA could leave more than $100 billion of demand for AI infrastructure gear unfulfilled next year because of supply constraints. | source: Analysis: What Nvidia’s Massive Supply-Demand Gap Says About AI Mania (crn.com) input gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n  - e1333 [third_party_view; 2026-07-31] Analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to grow 82% in FY2027. | source: Nobody's Talking About It, But This Business Could Make Nvidia a $10 Trillion Company (fool.com) input gnews:019ddb75bb67d2fb9b212f18\n  - e2147 [third_party_view; 2026-08-19] Yahoo! Finance data showed five upward and no downward analyst revisions to NVIDIA fiscal 2027 second-quarter estimates over the month before August 19, 2026. | source: Nvidia Guided to $91 Billion. Wall Street Penciled In $92 Billion. (fool.com) input gnews:712a161a59386d843542f6ac\n  - e2666 [t