pplied to the cited FY2027 base, modestly below the prior $678 billion consensus anchor; the implied range is therefore updated. The new evidence and updated export-control theme affect the balance of support but do not move the forecast across a rung boundary.\n- Latest reasoning: The market reference is analyst consensus of about $678 billion for FY2028, which sits at rung 2. The current implied outcome remains around $671–$678 billion: NVIDIA's 70% outlook is about $673 billion, while the analyst forecast is $678 billion; applying Zacks' 63.2% growth estimate to the cited $411 billion FY2027 estimate gives about $671 billion. These figures remain below the $700 billion rung-1 boundary. Chip-volume and customer-demand evidence, together with favorable export-control and capex themes, support the upper end, but supply and infrastructure constraints, earlier Huawei launches, and memory tightness temper the upside; none supplies a quantified revision that takes FY2028 revenue across $700 billion.\n- Evidence in force: 55 (party_statement 24, third_party_view 23, fact 8)\n- Evidence cited by the latest judgement:\n  - e4348 [third_party_view; 2026-09-10; push none] Analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of $411 billion in FY2027 and $678 billion in FY2028, implying 65% FY2028 growth. | source: Nvidia Has $96 Billion in Quarterly Revenue. Here's Why the Stock Is Still a Buy. (fool.com) input gnews:90f3858225bf7e19b8f38f21\n  - e4703 [third_party_view; 2026-09-14; push toward_last] Zacks consensus estimates NVIDIA FY2028 total revenue growth of 63.2% year over year and EPS growth of 63.8%. | source: NVIDIA vs. Marvell: Which AI Infrastructure Stock Is the Better Buy? (zacks.com) input gnews:1d3bc1ba4c2df5e998884bdb\n  - e4859 [party_statement; 2026-09-17; push toward_first] NVIDIA forecast 70% total revenue growth, to about $673 billion, in the fiscal year ending January 2028 (FY2028). | source: Jensen Huang says Nvidia will sell twice as many chips next year (cnbc.com) input gnews:f94df9a4bc981f0c32ba5797\n  - e3980 [party_statement; 2026-09-04; push toward_last] NVIDIA described its FY2028 sales outlook as constrained by chip production capacity rather than customer demand. | source: Prediction: Vera Rubin Is About to Become a $20 Billion Windfall for Nvidia by Next Quarter (fool.com) input gnews:bbd72d5fbff98d39746e6cb9\n  - e3993 [party_statement; 2026-09-05; push toward_last] NVIDIA warned that shortages of land, power, and other data-center infrastructure could delay customer hardware deployments. | source: Most Investors Overpay for AI Hype. Nvidia Is the Exception. (fool.com) input gnews:8653711909bcf63268b8735b\n  - e3939 [fact; 2026-09-04; push toward_first] Amazon ordered 2 million NVIDIA GPUs for delivery across 2027 and 2028. | source: Jensen Huang's Nvidia Guided for 70% Revenue Growth in Fiscal 2028, Far Above the 44% Wall Street Expected, as Amazon Agreed to Buy 2 Million Nvidia GPUs. Is the Growth Forecast Believable? (fool.com) input gnews:89698c9955cf8aa35b642970\n  - e4342 [party_statement; 2026-09-10; push toward_first] Amazon Web Services plans to deploy an additional 2 million GPUs through fiscal 2029, increasing its planned use of GPU infrastructure. | source: Nvidia Has $96 Billion in Quarterly Revenue. Here's Why the Stock Is Still a Buy. (fool.com) input gnews:90f3858225bf7e19b8f38f21\n  - e4858 [party_statement; 2026-09-17; push toward_first] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang forecast that NVIDIA would sell twice as many chips in 2027 as in 2026. | source: Jensen Huang says Nvidia will sell twice as many chips next year (cnbc.com) input gnews:f94df9a4bc981f0c32ba5797\n  - e4884 [fact; 2026-09-17; push toward_last] Huawei moved the planned release of its Ascend 960DT AI chip from Q4 2027 to Q1 2027, nine months earlier. | source: China's Homegrown AI Chip Push Just Got Faster. Is This a Real Threat to Nvidia? (fool.com) input gnews:90eeb17159f8e9139586875f\n  - e4885 [fact; 2026-09-17; push toward_last] Huawei moved the planned release of its Ascend 960PR AI chip from Q4 2027 to Q3 2027, three months earlier. | source: China's Homegrown AI Chip Push Just Got Faster. Is This a Real Threat to Nvidia? (fool.com) input gnews:90eeb17159f8e9139586875f\n  - e5027 [party_statement; 2026-09-19; push toward_last] Micron management said memory-chip market tightness should persist until 2028. | source: Better Artificial Intelligence (AI) Stock Pick for 2027: Nvidia versus Micron (fool.com) input gnews:4ee5d8f73b7bcfc2f2111ad1\n  - e5028 [third_party_view; 2026-09-19; push toward_first] Micron is building additional production facilities that the article says are likely to come online starting in mid-2027 and continuing through 2028. | source: Better Artificial Intelligence (AI) Stock Pick for 2027: Nvidia versus Micron (fool.com) input gnews:4ee5d8f73b7bcfc2f2111ad1\n  - e3994 [fact; 2026-09-05; push toward_first] Microsoft Azure revenue grew 43% year over year in Microsoft FY2026 Q4, ended June 30, 2026. | source: Most Investors Overpay for AI Hype. Nvidia Is the Exception. (fool.com) input gnews:8653711909bcf63268b8735b\n  - e3995 [fact; 2026-09-05; push toward_first] Amazon Web Services net sales increased 37% year over year in 2026 Q2. | source: Most Investors Overpay for AI Hype. Nvidia Is the Exception. (fool.com) input gnews:8653711909bcf63268b8735b\n  - e3996 [fact; 2026-09-05; push toward_first] Alphabet Google Cloud revenue grew 82% year over year in 2026 Q2, with Alphabet attributing growth to demand for AI infrastructure and solutions. | source: Most Investors Overpay for AI Hype. Nvidia Is the Exception. (fool.com) input gnews:8653711909bcf63268b8735b\n- A random sample of uncited evidence in force (seed 20261120):\n  - e4339 [fact; 2026-09-10] NVIDIA’s trailing-12-month revenue reached $303 billion, more than 11 times its 2022 level. | source: Nvidia Has $96 Billion in Quarterly Revenue. Here's Why the Stock Is Still a Buy. (fool.com) input gnews:90f3858225bf7e19b8f38f21\n  - e4156 [third_party_view; 2026-09-07] JPMorgan expects China's domestic AI compute demand to grow at about an 80% compound annual rate; the forecast period is not specified. | source: China’s Nvidia challenger crashed 20% in a reality check for an AI darling (businessinsider.com) input gnews:d6c518e6321240629a462792\n  - e4925 [party_statement; 2026-09-18] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang forecast that NVIDIA would sell roughly twice as many chips next year as this year, citing continued AI demand across industries. | source: Nvidia CEO Delivers Stunning Prediction About Chip Sales (gurufocus.com) input gnews:da7fc36177a5bfa60708297f\n  - e4245 [party_statement; 2026-09-09] NVIDIA said it plans to expand Australian AI-related data-centre capacity to up to 2 GW by 2027, more than doubling the nation's current load, through partnerships with Firmus, CDC, NEXTDC and AirTrunk. | source: Nvidia plans major expansion of data centre capacity in Australia to meet AI demand (reuters.com) input gnews:11f13514c1de829e7b70ea2b\n  - e4135 [third_party_view; 2026-09-06] Keithen Drury estimated NVIDIA trailing twelve-month revenue could reach $555 billion by approximately September 2027. | source: Nvidia Stock to Double Within a Year? Analyst Sees Market Cap Reaching $10.65 Trillion (finance.biggo.com) input gnews:a1001762888510be822dcfd8\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
