{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,80p' src/hivemind/bundle.py; ls -d .venv; rg -n 'show more|Load more|slice\\\\(|librarySelection' poc/ui/src/components/library.js; ls -a /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad | rg 'library|council|coher|intake'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3958,3984p;1256,1285p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n 'def open_read_only' src/hivemind; sed -n '55,135p;280,365p' src/hivemind/views/judging.py\"","aggregated_output":"## D51 · 2026-10-21 · Claude's open items settled: one re-judging rule, dependencies chosen in the matching call, no consensus\n\n- By: Alex, item by item. Asked which items were his to decide, he had Claude re-check the twelve open items Claude\n  had written in, against the latest design (\"for yourself to reiterate the issue in case you made stupid mistakes that\n  are not issues anymore in the latest version\"). Then: \"好，一个一个来问我\" (the nine no longer issues dropped); on\n  re-judging, \"A 可以但是设计逻辑要干净点；你思考下和我说\", then \"ok\"; on which views dependencies are chosen from,\n  \"ok\"; on consensus, \"What … is a consensus that you're talking about … Every time the evidence updates or whatever,\n  the ladder needs to be run by the model to determine whether it's going to shift from neutral to bearish or from\n  neutral to bullish … That's the logic\"; then \"可以你再仔细的对齐一次逻辑\". On the page: \"那你 FE 为什么写定稿了，这不是瞎写吗？\"\n- Decides:\n  1. Re-judging has one rule: a view is re-judged when what it reads changed. It reads its own evidence and the\n     conclusions (state and reasons) of the views it depends on. Its evidence changed when new evidence came or\n     evidence was replaced (a repeat alone does not count); a dependency's conclusion changed when that view's\n     judgement says so. Every judgement answers \"结论变不变\" in its fixed form: changed when the rung moved or a key fact\n     or number behind the state changed (AMZN's capex guidance from +12% to +25% inside one rung), unchanged when the\n     same thing is said again. Code checks only that a judgement that moved a rung, and the first judgement of a new\n     view, say changed. This gives Alex's \"如果美联储有重大的改动……确实需要重判\" (log step 10) to the model and\n     replaces the notice on a rung change only. A waiting view just built, and a dependency moving to its successor,\n     are cases of the same rule, so B is re-judged when its arrow moves to the next period (one of the details dropped\n     in D46 item 9, back as a case of this rule, as Claude told Alex before his \"ok\").\n  2. A new view's dependencies are chosen in the matching call (step 4), from the views the model already has in front\n     of it: the search results, the views listed in prompt part 5, and the views new in the same item; there is no\n     other search. In step 5 code checks that each is one of the views shown (or a year it waits for) and that no loop\n     forms. Writing into the views database has seven steps. Config holds two settings for the views database's model\n     calls (matching, re-judging), no longer a separate one for dependencies. A dependency on a view in none of the three\n     is missed, like a match the search misses; the records and the labels show it.\n  3. Consensus is not part of the design: a view has one state, judged by the model from its evidence whenever that\n     evidence changes (D46 item 1). The glossary row, the views notes and extraction's \"用来算共识\" go. Third-party views\n     stay evidence of their tier.\n  4. Open items are only what Alex deferred: how search ranks; the granularity of views, researched first (how many\n- Open for Alex: the seven items at the head of `docs/DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## D368 · 2026-11-05 · Alex's answers to the seven items left open by the consolidation\n\n- Alex, on the seven items at the head of `docs/DECISIONS.md` (D367): \"1. 这个你记住，我们要做 2. 做 3. 好那就按照后面的那条来 4. 好你来定 5. 你要来帮我看到底做不做\n  6. 你看该怎么处理核实 7. 不，用英文吧。\"; then \"你开始逐条改，不要drift, 记录下来把1-7都清理了我们再commit push,开始快速做\".\n- Decided:\n  1. The asset-thesis rungs stated against guidance, each thesis naming its favourable end (D186), and the rename of `industry_aggregate`\n     to `shared_quantity` (D191 point 4) are built in the next extraction version. The frozen v74i stays until then (D274); the new\n     version is measured against it.\n  2. The three decided rules not yet built are built, each designed and measured as its own slice (AGENTS §2, §7): a company's own\n     quantity is a thesis under that company, private companies included (D187); a later item may add a dependency to an existing thesis\n     (D191 point 2); the matching step chooses a new thesis's dependencies (D51), which the default Jev path does not ask today.\n  3. At the due day pull mode closes the due questions and does nothing else (D356); D248 boundary 2's step that opens the next-deadline\n     successor of an event question falling due unresolved is dropped.\n  4. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation, by D208's design: a seed question's dependency arrow means \"supports\". For filing, the\n     supporting (driver) question is the narrower one, so a statement linked to both goes to it, as `extraction.narrowest_links` does\n     today. For judging, the supported (root) question reads the supporting questions' conclusions, so drivers and themes are judged\n     before their roots. Today the judging code reads the stored edge the other way: the driver reads the root and is judged after it\n     (`seeding.seed_views` stores the seed's `depends_on` as the driver's dependency). The fix separates the two uses of the edge; it\n     changes judgements, so it is measured before it enters the default.\n  5. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation: PRD 10 is corrected without changing any rule. §4 names the frozen standard's version 5 and\n     §5 carries a status line (its links-rule version failed in §8 step 5; D361 keeps the fallback sentence).\n  6. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation: the three statements of the frozen extraction standard page that later decisions changed are\n     noted in a dated correction record beside it, `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard-corrections.md`; the page is not edited (D261). Each\n     statement was found verbatim in the page: \"抽取看不到库\" (§4 and §5.3; changed by D251 and D264), \"研究的交付物是论证\" (§7; the\n     argument record set aside on 2026-11-04) and \"只有事实能确定落在哪一档\" (§5 and §7; changed by D260 and D263).\nsrc/hivemind/views/store.py:219:def open_read_only(path):\n    require_supported(prompt_version)\n    pushes = PUSHES\n    schema = {\n        'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,\n        'required': ['rung', 'reasons', 'cites', 'cites_views', 'pushes', 'changed', 'why_changed'],\n        'properties': {\n            'rung': {'type': 'integer'}, 'reasons': {'type': 'string'},\n            'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}, 'cites_views': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}},\n            'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['evidence_id', 'push'],\n                                                  'properties': {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}},\n            'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': {'type': 'string'},\n        },\n    }\n    schema['required'].append('theme_pushes')\n    schema['properties']['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['view_id', 'push'],\n                                                                       'properties': {'view_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}}\n    schema['required'][1:1] = STANCE_FIELDS           # after rung: the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\n    schema['properties'].update({field: {'type': 'string'} for field in STANCE_FIELDS})\n    return schema\n\n\ndef themes_in_force(conn, view_id):\n    \"\"\"The theme block of an asset thesis: every open theme thesis with a current state, with its rung label and whether a\n    changed conclusion was recorded after this thesis's last judgement. Empty for a theme thesis.\"\"\"\n    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n        return []\n    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n    out = []\n    for row in conn.execute(\"select view_id from views where object_kind='theme' order by view_id\"):\n        theme_id = row['view_id']\n        state = store.current_state(conn, theme_id)\n        if not state or not store.is_open(conn, theme_id):\n            continue\n        updated = bool(last) and bool(conn.execute('select 1 from judgements where view_id=? and changed=1 and judgement_id>? limit 1',\n                                                   (theme_id, last['judgement_id'])).fetchone())\n        rung = store.rungs_of(conn, theme_id)[state['rung'] - 1]\n        out.append({'view_id': theme_id, 'view': store.view(conn, theme_id), 'state': state, 'rung_label': rung['label'], 'updated': updated})\n    return out\n\n\nSTANCE_FIELDS = ['reference', 'implied_outcome']   # D260: what the market expects, and the figure or date the evidence implies\n\n\nclass JudgementRefused(Exception):\n    pass\n\n\ndef topological(conn, view_ids):\n    \"\"\"Dependencies first: a view comes after every view it depends on that is also in the set.\"\"\"\n    remaining = list(dict.fromkeys(view_ids))\n    ordered, placed = [], set()\n    while remaining:\n        progressed = False\n        for view_id in list(remaining):\n            deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}\n            if deps.isdisjoint(set(remaining) - {view_id}) or deps <= placed:\n                ordered.append(view_id)\n                placed.add(view_id)\n                remaining.remove(view_id)\n                progressed = True\n        if not progressed:                 # a cycle slipped through: keep going in the given order\n            ordered.extend(remaining)\n            break\n    return ordered\n\n\ndef _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes=(), hidden=0):\n    \"\"\"hidden: how many pieces in force are not shown.\"\"\"\n    lines = [f'Thesis {view_id} ({v[\"object_id\"]}, {v[\"kind\"]}, focus \"{v[\"looks_at\"]}\", {v[\"year\"] or \"\"}, due {v[\"due_day\"]}): {v[\"question\"]}',\n             'Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {r[\"position\"]} {r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in rungs), '',\n             f'[Evidence in view under this thesis, {len(pieces)} items]']\n    if hidden:\n        lines.append(f'[Not shown: {hidden} more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]')\n    for p in pieces:\n        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n        if p.get('replaced'):\n            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\"replaced\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"replaced\"][\"original_day\"]}): {p[\"replaced\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n        if p.get('same_as'):\n            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\", \".join(p[\"same_as\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\n        if p.get('revises'):\n        queued.extend(queued_by_change(conn, row['view_id']))\n    return queued\n\n\ndef round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, changed_views, seq, item, *, transport=None):\n    \"\"\"Judge the open views in changed_views, dependencies first; a changed conclusion queues open dependants.\n\n    Views that do not depend on each other are judged at the same time: each level of the dependency order is sent\n    to the model concurrently (the prompts are built and the answers checked and written in this thread, so the\n    database connection never crosses threads). A view waits while anything upstream of it is still pending, so a\n    dependant always reads this round's conclusion of its dependency. A view with no evidence in force stays\n    unjudged (D59), and a view already judged at this sequence number (a resumed round) is not judged twice.\n\n    Among the views ready to be judged, theme theses go first, so an asset thesis reads this round's theme conclusions; a theme judgement that says changed queues every open asset thesis with\n    evidence in force. The starting queue adds what the ledger says earlier commits at this sequence number queued.\"\"\"\n    import concurrent.futures\n\n    version = cfg.rejudging.prompt_version\n    schema = schema_for(version)\n\n    def eligible(view_id):\n        return store.is_open(conn, view_id) and not store.has_judgement(conn, view_id, seq) and bool(store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id))\n\n    def is_theme(view_id):\n        return store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme'\n\n    pending = [v for v in topological(conn, list(changed_views) + queued_by_ledger(conn, seq)) if eligible(v)]\n    done, results = set(), []\n    while pending:\n        ready = [v for v in pending if upstream(conn, v).isdisjoint(set(pending) - {v})] or pending[:1]\n        level = [v for v in ready if is_theme(v)] or ready\n        prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, version) for v in level}\n\n        def ask(view_id, note=''):\n            system, user = prompts[view_id]\n            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schema, 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)\n\n        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:\n            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))\n        for view_id in level:\n            answer = answers[view_id]\n            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n            if errors:\n                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\n                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(errors))\n                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n                if errors:\n                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\n                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\n            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)\n            done.add(view_id)\n            results.append(result)\n            if result['changed']:\n                for dependant in queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n                    if dependant not in done and dependant not in pending and eligible(dependant):\n                        pending.append(dependant)\n        pending = [v for v in topological(conn, pending) if v not in done and eligible(v)]\n    return results\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,80p' src/hivemind/bundle.py; ls -d .venv; rg -n 'show more|Load more|slice\\\\(|librarySelection' poc/ui/src/components/library.js; ls -a /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad | rg 'library|council|coher|intake'\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"One view in the shape the front end reads: the ladder, every judgement round with the model's reason and the\nevidence it cited, the evidence in force with tiers, speakers and sources, dependencies, replacements and the freeze\nswitches. The same shaping writes the mock's data file (scripts/mock_data.py) and answers POST /ideas, so the front\nend's adapter reads both. Read-only on every database. With `as_of`, rows written after that day are left out.\"\"\"\nimport json\nfrom contextlib import contextmanager\nfrom datetime import date\n\nfrom . import service\nfrom .views import store\n\n\n@contextmanager\ndef read_snapshot(*connections):\n    \"\"\"Pin each read connection for a complete envelope; preserve a caller's transaction.\"\"\"\n    owned = []\n    try:\n        for conn in connections:\n            if conn is not None and not conn.in_transaction:\n                conn.execute('begin')\n                owned.append(conn)\n        yield\n    finally:\n        for conn in reversed(owned):\n            conn.rollback()\n\n\ndef item_lookup(items_db):\n    \"\"\"input id → title, publisher and category of a stored item, from the items database (or the id alone when the\n    database is not given or does not hold it).\"\"\"\n    cache = {}\n\n    def item_of(input_id):\n        if input_id not in cache:\n            row = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, publisher_type, category, publication_day, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone() if items_db is not None else None\n            cache[input_id] = dict(row) if row else {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'publisher_type': '', 'category': '', 'publication_day': '', 'source_uri': ''}\n        return cache[input_id]\n    return item_of\n\n\ndef _visible(views_db, seq, as_of):\n    return as_of is None or service.visible(views_db, seq, as_of)\n\n\ndef ladder_row(views_db, view_id):\n    \"\"\"The view's ladder as the new system's writer stored it (`clean_ladders`, written in the view's own call): the parsed\n    ladder; 'no table' for a store without that table (a legacy ledger); 'no row' when the store has the table and no row for the\n    view. A row that is not readable JSON with a ladder, or two rows for one view, is refused.\"\"\"\n    if not views_db.execute(\"select 1 from sqlite_master where type='table' and name='clean_ladders'\").fetchone():\n        return 'no table'\n    rows = views_db.execute('select checked_answer from clean_ladders where view_id=?', (view_id,)).fetchall()\n    if not rows:\n        return 'no row'\n    if len(rows) > 1:\n        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: {len(rows)} ladder rows for one view')\n    try:\n        ladder = json.loads(rows[0][0])['ladder']\n    except (TypeError, ValueError, KeyError) as error:\n        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row holds no readable ladder ({error!r})')\n    if not isinstance(ladder, dict):\n        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its ladder row holds no readable ladder')\n    return ladder\n\n\ndef not_judged(views_db, view_id, created_seq, as_of=None):\n    \"\"\"D397: the parts of a topic its one judged question leaves out, with their reasons, from the view's ladder row. None for a\n    legacy ledger, for a view with no row, and before the view's creation at as_of; [] when the row lists none. A malformed row,\n    or two rows for one view, is refused. Called directly for a view not visible at the resolved bound, it refuses the view\n    (OPERATING-CONTRACT.md, row 3), so a question created after that day is never returned.\"\"\"\n    as_of = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of, unfiltered=True)\n    if as_of is not None and not _visible(views_db, created_seq, as_of):\n        raise KeyError(f'{view_id} is not available as of {as_of}')\n    ladder = ladder_row(views_db, view_id)\n    if ladder in ('no table', 'no row'):\n        return None\n    parts = ladder.get('not_judged')\n    if not isinstance(parts, list) or not all(isinstance(p, dict) and isinstance(p.get('part'), str) and isinstance(p.get('why'), str) for p in parts):\n        raise ValueError(f'{view_id}: its parts not judged are not a list of {{part, why}} texts')\n    return [{'part': p['part'], 'why': p['why']} for p in parts]\n\nls: .venv: No such file or directory\n2:import { librarySelection, libraryCounts } from '../model/library.js';\n90:        librarySelection(data, { day: state.day, group: 'ungrouped' }).length,\n94:    const rows = librarySelection(data, state);\n101:    for (const thesis of rows.slice(0, state.limit)) {\napi-library.json\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sqlite3 -readonly poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite '.schema calls'; sqlite3 -readonly poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite '.schema dependencies'; sed -n '136,198p' src/hivemind/views/judging.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sqlite3 -readonly poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite '.schema calls'; sqlite3 -readonly poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite '.schema dependencies'; sed -n '136,198p' src/hivemind/views/judging.py\"","aggregated_output":"CREATE TABLE dependencies (dependency_id integer primary key autoincrement, view_id text, depends_on text, wait_chain_view_id text, wait_year text, direction text, seq integer);\nCREATE TRIGGER dependencies_no_update before update on dependencies begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end;\nCREATE TRIGGER dependencies_no_delete before delete on dependencies begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end;\nCREATE INDEX deps_view on dependencies(view_id);\n            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n    if deps:\n        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n        for d in deps:\n            target = d['resolved_to']\n            if not target:\n                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n                continue\n            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n    if themes:\n        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n        for theme in themes:\n            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n    if last:\n        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n    else:\n        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n    return lines\n\n\ndef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n    require_supported(prompt_version)\n    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\n    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n    pieces, hidden = evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)\n    deps = store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id)\n    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n    lines = _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes_in_force(conn, view_id), hidden=hidden)\n    with open(config.prompt_path(prompt_version + '.txt'), encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n        return handle.read(), '\\n'.join(lines)\n\n\ndef retry_note(errors):\n    return '\\n\\nThe code returned the previous answer because: ' + '; '.join(errors) + '\\nCorrect it and answer again, citing only the listed ids.'\n\n\ndef themes_shown_in(request_text):\n    \"\"\"The theme ids of the block a request carried: the ids the answer may name, whatever the ledger says now.\"\"\"\n    block = request_text.split('\\n[Themes in force, ', 1)\n    return set(re.findall(r'^- (v\\d+) \\(', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n\n\ndef evidence_shown_in(request_text):\n    \"\"\"The evidence ids the request listed: the ids the answer may cite and push.\"\"\"\n    block = request_text.split('\\n[Evidence in ', 1)\n    return set(re.findall(r'^- (e\\d+) \\[', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n\n\ndef check_answer(conn, view_id, data, request_text=None):\n    \"\"\"request_text: the user message that was sent, so theme and evidence ids are checked against what it carried (a theme may have\n    closed or opened since); without it, against what the ledger would show now.\"\"\"\n    errors = []\n    shown = themes_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {theme['view_id'] for theme in themes_in_force(conn, view_id)}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3, json, re\nfrom hivemind import bundle, service\nbase=Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17'\\\\'')\nitems=sqlite3.connect((base/'\\\\''items-comparison.sqlite'\\\\'').resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\nitems.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\nchoices={1:('\\\\''v4'\\\\'','\\\\''v8'\\\\''),2:('\\\\''v8'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v17'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'','\\\\''v35'\\\\''),3:('\\\\''v3'\\\\'','\\\\''v35'\\\\'')}\nfor run, vids in choices.items():\n with service.open_ledger(base/f'\\\\''run/old-{run}/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'') as db:\n  data=bundle.library(db,items,'\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\'')\n  vs={v['\\\\''view_id'\\\\'']:v for v in data['\\\\''views'\\\\'']}\n  print('\\\\''old'\\\\'',run,'\\\\''views'\\\\'',len(vs),'\\\\''deps'\\\\'',sum(bool(v['\\\\''dependencies'\\\\'']) for v in vs.values()),'\\\\''judgements'\\\\'',sum(len(v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\'']) for v in vs.values()),'\\\\''citing others'\\\\'',sum(bool(j['\\\\''cited_views'\\\\'']) for v in vs.values() for j in v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\'']))\n  for vid in vids:\n   v=vs[vid]; j=v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\''][-1]\n   print(vid, j['\\\\''day'\\\\''],j['\\\\''id'\\\\''],j['\\\\''seq'\\\\''],v['\\\\''question'\\\\''])\n   print(j['\\\\''reasons'\\\\''])\n   if run==3: print('\\\\''bands'\\\\'',v['\\\\''rungs'\\\\''])\n  if run==2:\n   v=vs['\\\\''v9'\\\\'']\n   for j in v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\'']:\n    if j['\\\\''day'\\\\''] in ('\\\\''2026-09-12'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-13'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-14'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-15'\\\\''): print('\\\\''shift'\\\\'',j['\\\\''day'\\\\''],j['\\\\''reasons'\\\\''])\n   print('\\\\''414 items'\\\\'',[(e['\\\\''id'\\\\''],e['\\\\''one_line'\\\\''][:125]) for e in v['\\\\''evidence'\\\\''] if re.search(r'\\\\''(?<\"'!'\"\\\\d)414(?\"'!'\"\\\\d)'\\\\'',e['\\\\''one_line'\\\\'']+'\\\\'' '\\\\''+e['\\\\''quote'\\\\''])])\n   print('\\\\''counts'\\\\'',[(vid,sum(a['\\\\''rung'\\\\'']\"'!=b['\"'\\\\''rung'\\\\''] for a,b in zip(vs[vid]['\\\\''judgements'\\\\''],vs[vid]['\\\\''judgements'\\\\''][1:]))) for vid in ('\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v8'\\\\'','\\\\''v5'\\\\'','\\\\''v10'\\\\'')])\n   for v in sorted(vs.values(), key=lambda v: ((v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''day'\\\\''] if v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\''] else v['\\\\''created_day'\\\\'']),v['\\\\''created_seq'\\\\'']), reverse=True)[:5]:\n    print('\\\\''rank'\\\\'',v['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''],v['\\\\''question'\\\\''])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -c 'from pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3, json, re\nfrom hivemind import bundle, service\nbase=Path('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17'\\\\'')\nitems=sqlite3.connect((base/'\\\\''items-comparison.sqlite'\\\\'').resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\'',uri=True)\nitems.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\nchoices={1:('\\\\''v4'\\\\'','\\\\''v8'\\\\''),2:('\\\\''v8'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v14'\\\\'','\\\\''v16'\\\\'','\\\\''v17'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'','\\\\''v35'\\\\''),3:('\\\\''v3'\\\\'','\\\\''v35'\\\\'')}\nfor run, vids in choices.items():\n with service.open_ledger(base/f'\\\\''run/old-{run}/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'') as db:\n  data=bundle.library(db,items,'\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\'')\n  vs={v['\\\\''view_id'\\\\'']:v for v in data['\\\\''views'\\\\'']}\n  print('\\\\''old'\\\\'',run,'\\\\''views'\\\\'',len(vs),'\\\\''deps'\\\\'',sum(bool(v['\\\\''dependencies'\\\\'']) for v in vs.values()),'\\\\''judgements'\\\\'',sum(len(v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\'']) for v in vs.values()),'\\\\''citing others'\\\\'',sum(bool(j['\\\\''cited_views'\\\\'']) for v in vs.values() for j in v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\'']))\n  for vid in vids:\n   v=vs[vid]; j=v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\''][-1]\n   print(vid, j['\\\\''day'\\\\''],j['\\\\''id'\\\\''],j['\\\\''seq'\\\\''],v['\\\\''question'\\\\''])\n   print(j['\\\\''reasons'\\\\''])\n   if run==3: print('\\\\''bands'\\\\'',v['\\\\''rungs'\\\\''])\n  if run==2:\n   v=vs['\\\\''v9'\\\\'']\n   for j in v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\'']:\n    if j['\\\\''day'\\\\''] in ('\\\\''2026-09-12'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-13'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-14'\\\\'','\\\\''2026-09-15'\\\\''): print('\\\\''shift'\\\\'',j['\\\\''day'\\\\''],j['\\\\''reasons'\\\\''])\n   print('\\\\''414 items'\\\\'',[(e['\\\\''id'\\\\''],e['\\\\''one_line'\\\\''][:125]) for e in v['\\\\''evidence'\\\\''] if re.search(r'\\\\''(?<\"'!'\"\\\\d)414(?\"'!'\"\\\\d)'\\\\'',e['\\\\''one_line'\\\\'']+'\\\\'' '\\\\''+e['\\\\''quote'\\\\''])])\n   print('\\\\''counts'\\\\'',[(vid,sum(a['\\\\''rung'\\\\'']\"'!=b['\"'\\\\''rung'\\\\''] for a,b in zip(vs[vid]['\\\\''judgements'\\\\''],vs[vid]['\\\\''judgements'\\\\''][1:]))) for vid in ('\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''v8'\\\\'','\\\\''v5'\\\\'','\\\\''v10'\\\\'')])\n   for v in sorted(vs.values(), key=lambda v: ((v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\''][-1]['\\\\''day'\\\\''] if v['\\\\''judgements'\\\\''] else v['\\\\''created_day'\\\\'']),v['\\\\''created_seq'\\\\'']), reverse=True)[:5]:\n    print('\\\\''rank'\\\\'',v['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''],v['\\\\''question'\\\\''])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"old 1 views 47 deps 0 judgements 1609 citing others 0\nv4 2026-09-20 1575 1884 What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\nThe market reference is Wall Street consensus of about $411 billion, which is rung 2. NVIDIA's stated 70% full-year growth outlook implies about $367 billion from FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion (rung 3), but the current-quarter guidance and the specific Q4 growth estimate imply a higher outcome: about $404 billion. That is above rung 3's $392 billion boundary but below rung 1's $431.2 billion threshold. Supply constraints and competition temper the upside; the evidence does not imply enough additional revenue to cross rung 1.\nv8 2026-09-20 1580 1884 How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\nThe reference is Morningstar’s $361 billion FY2027 Data Center estimate, which is in rung 2. The implied outcome is higher, at about $390 billion, but remains below rung 1’s $400 billion boundary: the reported first half is $164 billion, Q3 is about $100 billion using the $108 billion total-revenue midpoint and the recent 92.5% Data Center mix, and I estimate Q4 at about $126 billion, allowing for the stated Q4 reacceleration and Vera Rubin supply build while discounting for supply and infrastructure constraints. Thus the evidence supports a substantial premium to the reference but does not imply crossing $400 billion.\nold 2 views 43 deps 0 judgements 1616 citing others 0\nv8 2026-09-20 1616 1884 How much revenue will NVIDIA generate from stand-alone CPU sales in FY2027?\nThe reference is NVIDIA's roughly $20 billion FY2027 stand-alone CPU sales guidance, which sits at rung 2; no separate market-consensus figure is supplied. The evidence supports a substantial ramp but still implies about $18 billion: Wolfe's estimate of 1.3 million Vera chips at about $5,000 each is roughly $6.5 billion, while AWS's CPU quantity is only described as millions without a purchase period and OCI's hundreds-of-thousands plan is not a FY2027 revenue figure. These disclosures, alongside shipments underway, support growth beyond the tracked base but do not establish the roughly 4 million units needed for $20 billion at that ASP. Thus the implied figure remains below the rung-2 boundary and within rung 3. The FY2028 doubling outlook is not a FY2027 estimate, and AWS receiving its first server improves evidence of execution without quantifying the FY2027 volume enough to move the forecast across a boundary.\nv9 2026-09-20 1592 1884 How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\nThe market reference is approximately $414 billion for FY2027, which is rung 2. The evidence-based estimate is now around $410 billion: NVIDIA reported $164 billion in the first half, Q3 total-revenue guidance and the recent Data Center mix imply roughly $100 billion for Q3, and a roughly $146 billion Q4 is supported by the expected hyperscale reacceleration and Rubin ramp. SemiAnalysis's forecast of second-half Data Center revenue 20% above analyst estimates is a meaningful upside input: applying it to the roughly $250 billion of second-half revenue implied by the $414 billion reference would point to about $464 billion for the year. I discount that forecast because it does not state its underlying estimate and its implied Q4 is much higher than the company has quantified; the resulting central estimate remains near $410 billion. That crosses the $400 billion boundary into rung 2, but not the $450 billion boundary. Supply and competition risks, and NVIDIA's exclusion of China compute revenue from its outlook, temper the upside.\nv14 2026-09-20 1585 1884 How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\nThe reference is about $411 billion for FY2027, which sits at rung 2; the cited Zacks growth estimate also implies about $405 billion using FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion. The operating run-rate implies about $419 billion: estimate Q3 at roughly $113.5 billion by applying the cited average 3.1% beat to the $110.16 billion high end of guidance, then carry the guided 12% sequential growth forward to Q4, about $127 billion, alongside reported Q1 and Q2 revenue. Supply constraints are a meaningful downside risk, but the cited estimate of more than $100 billion in unfulfilled demand is for “next year” and is not quantified as a reduction to FY2027 revenue. The implied outcome remains above $400 billion and below $450 billion, so it stays at rung 2.\nv16 2026-09-20 1596 1884 How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA generate in FY2027?\nThe reference is NVIDIA’s approximately $20 billion FY2027 standalone CPU outlook, which sits at rung 3. The most likely total is just above $25 billion: the specific FY2027 Vera outlook is about $20 billion, and Grace had already exceeded $5 billion on a trailing-12-month basis during FY2027; carrying that recent Grace run-rate through the fiscal year puts the total slightly above the rung-1 boundary. Vera shipments and full production support the outlook, though the estimate is close to the boundary: Wolfe’s 2026 shipment estimate implies about $6.5 billion for calendar 2026, and AMD’s performance claims are competitive risks without a quantified revision to NVIDIA’s FY2027 outlook. The approximately $20 billion server-CPU demand figure is a headwind, but it is not an explicit cap on NVIDIA’s specific Vera sales outlook.\nv17 2026-09-20 1586 1884 How much will NVIDIA's total revenue grow in FY2028?\nThe company’s approximately 70% FY2028 growth guidance is the primary reference and sits at rung 1; the more recent analyst estimates of 63.2%–65.5% also sit at rung 1, while the 44% LSEG estimate is a rung-3 counterweight. The implied outcome remains about 70%: NVIDIA says supply supports that growth, while demand is higher. The newer forecast of twice as many chips sold in calendar 2027 supports strong volume but does not translate directly into FY2028 revenue growth or displace the company’s supply-constrained outlook. The implied outcome stays above the 60% rung boundary.\nv21 2026-09-20 1599 1884 How much will NVIDIA's total revenue grow in FY2027?\nThe market reference is roughly 87–90% FY2027 growth (Zacks estimates 87.4–88%, while the $411 billion estimate implies about 90% against FY2026 revenue), which is rung 1; the ladder's cited 42% estimate is not the current reference. Q1 and Q2 revenue plus Q3 guidance total $285.8 billion. Carrying forward the approximately 12% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance gives Q4 revenue of about $121 billion, FY2027 revenue near $407 billion, and growth of about 88% from FY2026's $215.94 billion. The CFO's approximately 70% growth outlook implies about $367 billion, also rung 1. Supplier constraints temper the faster run-rate case, but the reported results and Q3 guide still imply growth well above the 60% boundary.\nv35 2026-09-20 1608 1884 How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028?\nThe market reference is analyst consensus of about $678 billion for FY2028, which sits at rung 2. The current implied outcome remains around $671–$678 billion: NVIDIA's 70% outlook is about $673 billion, while the analyst forecast is $678 billion; applying Zacks' 63.2% growth estimate to the cited $411 billion FY2027 estimate gives about $671 billion. These figures remain below the $700 billion rung-1 boundary. Chip-volume and customer-demand evidence, together with favorable export-control and capex themes, support the upper end, but supply and infrastructure constraints, earlier Huawei launches, and memory tightness temper the upside; none supplies a quantified revision that takes FY2028 revenue across $700 billion.\nshift 2026-09-12 The reference is approximately $372 billion, which sits in rung 3. The evidence-based estimate is about $414 billion: FY2027 Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25 billion; the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide, applying the latest 92.5% Data Center mix, implies about $99.9 billion for Q3. Retaining the prior H2 analyst baseline of about $208 billion and applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside gives about $249.6 billion for H2, or roughly $414 billion for FY2027. This clears rung 2’s $400 billion floor but not rung 1’s $450 billion floor. Rubin production shipments, purchase orders, and customer-side utilization evidence support demand, while no new quantified FY2027 estimate establishes enough additional revenue to cross $450 billion; the stated 70% supply figure concerns FY2028 growth.\nshift 2026-09-13 The market reference is approximately $372 billion, which sits at rung 3. The evidence-based estimate is about $414 billion: FY2027 Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25 billion; the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $100 billion of Data Center revenue at the latest 92.5% mix, and the carried H2 analyst baseline of about $208 billion, raised 20% by SemiAnalysis's H2 forecast, implies about $249.6 billion for H2. Q3 is included in H2, so it is not added again. The resulting FY2027 estimate clears rung 2's $400 billion floor but remains below rung 1's $450 billion floor. Recent customer utilization and Oracle deployment evidence reinforce demand, while the new information does not quantify enough additional FY2027 revenue to move the estimate across the $450 billion boundary; competitor investment and custom-chip development remain offsets.\nshift 2026-09-14 The approximately $414 billion forecast is above rung 2’s $400 billion floor but below rung 1’s $450 billion floor. Strong growth, the Q3 guide, and demand evidence support the estimate, but the new customer commitments span multiple years and cannot be counted in full for FY2027. China revenue is excluded from NVIDIA’s forward outlook, and competing accelerator supply is a further offset; the evidence does not imply enough incremental FY2027 revenue to cross $450 billion.\nshift 2026-09-15 The reference is an approximately $414 billion FY2027 expectation, which sits in rung 2. The latest reported quarter and near-term outlook imply a lower run-rate: Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25 billion; applying the recent 92.5% Data Center mix to NVIDIA's $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide gives about $100 billion for Q3. Carrying that growth into Q4, with management's stated Q4 reacceleration, implies roughly $115 billion for Q4 and about $379 billion for FY2027. The demand evidence and Rubin ramp support growth, but the disclosed multi-year commitments cannot be counted fully in FY2027, and China compute revenue is excluded from the outlook. The resulting estimate is below $400 billion but above $350 billion, so it crosses from the reference's rung 2 to rung 3.\n414 items []\ncounts [('v9', 8), ('v8', 8), ('v5', 5), ('v10', 6)]\nrank v43 Will the required U.S. and EU regulatory reviews of NVIDIA's Hugging Face acquisition be cleared by 2027-06-30?\nrank v42 Will the AI Energy Management Alliance's first power-flexible AI data center in Manassas secure faster grid interconnection terms or preferential tariffs by 2026-12-31?\nrank v40 Will NVIDIA invest $10 billion to anchor Anthropic's IPO by 2026-09-20?\nrank v39 Will the U.S. Justice Department conclude its antitrust review of NVIDIA’s Groq transaction by 2027-01-31?\nrank v38 Will NVIDIA complete an investment of roughly $2.5 billion to $3 billion in Thinking Machines Lab by 2027-09-04?\nold 3 views 49 deps 0 judgements 1707 citing others 0\nv3 2026-09-20 1672 1884 What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?\nThe market reference is about $411 billion (e4360, e5406), which sits in rung 2 ($392 billion to below $431.2 billion). The evidence-based run-rate is about $419 billion before the additional second-half data-center-compute uplift: first-half revenue was $177.837 billion; Q3 is about $113.6 billion using the $108 billion midpoint guidance and the cited 3.1% average beat over the high end; carrying the guided 12% sequential growth pace forward gives about $127 billion for Q4. Applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% uplift only to second-half data-center compute adds about $27–28 billion, implying roughly $446 billion and crossing the rung-1 boundary. The analyst view of 90% Q3 and 65% Q4 year-over-year growth is a counter-signal, but it does not outweigh the guided-growth run-rate and the specific second-half compute tracking. The 70% full-year growth statement would imply about $367 billion from FY2026 revenue, but that would require a sharp Q4 decline after the reported first half and Q3 guidance, so it is inconsistent with the nearer-term run-rate.\nbands [{'position': 1, 'label': 'Strongly bullish', 'condition': 'Total revenue is at least $431.2 billion (110% of the $392 billion analyst estimate).', 'lo': 431200000000.0, 'hi': None}, {'position': 2, 'label': 'Bullish', 'condition': 'Total revenue is at least $392 billion and below $431.2 billion.', 'lo': 392000000000.0, 'hi': 431200000000.0}, {'position': 3, 'label': 'Neutral', 'condition': 'Total revenue is at least $352.8 billion and below $392 billion (within 10% below the analyst estimate).', 'lo': 352800000000.0, 'hi': 392000000000.0}, {'position': 4, 'label': 'Bearish', 'condition': 'Total revenue is at least $313.6 billion and below $352.8 billion.', 'lo': 313600000000.0, 'hi': 352800000000.0}, {'position': 5, 'label': 'Strongly bearish', 'condition': 'Total revenue is below $313.6 billion (more than 20% below the analyst estimate).', 'lo': None, 'hi': 313600000000.0}]\nv35 2026-09-20 1674 1884 What will NVIDIA report as data-center revenue for FY2027?\nThe only supplied quantified market reference is Morningstar's $361 billion FY2027 estimate, which sits exactly at rung 2's floor. The implied outcome is about $374–375 billion: NVIDIA reported $164 billion in the first half; the Q3 outlook of about $108 billion in total revenue, applied to the latest 92.5% Data Center mix, implies about $100 billion of Data Center revenue; and roughly $110 billion in Q4 is consistent with management's expected reacceleration and the supplied forecast of more than $100 billion. That is above rung 2's $361 billion floor but below rung 1's $400 billion threshold; the new demand and supply evidence does not quantify enough additional FY2027 revenue to bridge the gap.\nbands [{'position': 1, 'label': 'Strongly bullish', 'condition': 'FY2027 data-center revenue is at least $400 billion.', 'lo': 400000000000.0, 'hi': None}, {'position': 2, 'label': 'Bullish', 'condition': 'FY2027 data-center revenue is at least $361 billion but less than $400 billion.', 'lo': 361000000000.0, 'hi': 400000000000.0}, {'position': 3, 'label': 'Neutral', 'condition': 'FY2027 data-center revenue is at least $300 billion but less than $361 billion.', 'lo': 300000000000.0, 'hi': 361000000000.0}, {'position': 4, 'label': 'Bearish', 'condition': 'FY2027 data-center revenue is at least $250 billion but less than $300 billion.', 'lo': 250000000000.0, 'hi': 300000000000.0}, {'position': 5, 'label': 'Strongly bearish', 'condition': 'FY2027 data-center revenue is less than $250 billion.', 'lo': None, 'hi': 250000000000.0}]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
