estion falling due unresolved is dropped.\n  3973\t  4. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation, by D208's design: a seed question's dependency arrow means \"supports\". For filing, the\n  3974\t     supporting (driver) question is the narrower one, so a statement linked to both goes to it, as `extraction.narrowest_links` does\n  3975\t     today. For judging, the supported (root) question reads the supporting questions' conclusions, so drivers and themes are judged\n  3976\t     before their roots. Today the judging code reads the stored edge the other way: the driver reads the root and is judged after it\n  3977\t     (`seeding.seed_views` stores the seed's `depends_on` as the driver's dependency). The fix separates the two uses of the edge; it\n  3978\t     changes judgements, so it is measured before it enters the default.\n  3979\t  5. Settled by Claude on Alex's delegation: PRD 10 is corrected without changing any rule. §4 names the frozen standard's version 5 and\n    46\t\n    47\t## Recommendation and one test (consensus)\n    48\t1. **$0 first:** serve a copy of old-2's finished 09-20 store (43 questions, 42 open) with its articles locally on the page, API and\n    49\t   MCP, confirm all three show the same day and source links (the page silently keeps its embedded v34 copy if its fetch fails), and\n    50\t   Alex reads it for half an hour: would an analyst use this? Codex read the store through the shared reader (`bundle.py:225`): it\n    51\t   returns 09-20 and all 43 questions.\n    52\t2. **Only if he says yes:** build the daily wrapper (harvest → clean → append → replay one day → snapshot → publish) with its alerts,\n    53\t   rehearse it one day at a time over the harvested 09-21..09-27 with one deliberately failed day (about $0.60 at the measured rate),\n    54\t   then plan the gap after 10-27 and switch to real days.\n    55\t\n    56\t## Step 1 done (2026-11-20)\n    28\t        .join(' ')\n    29\t        .toLocaleLowerCase();\n    30\t      